      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 0,
      "text": "301. Letters Orders and, Instructions. December 1755. 5,",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line000.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 1,
      "text": "be sure of indemnity. If your Honor would",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line001.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 2,
      "text": "be kind enough to intimate this to General",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line002.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 3,
      "text": "Shirley, or the Colonels of those Regiments,- it",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line003.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 4,
      "text": "would be of Service to us: without leave, we",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line004.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 5,
      "text": "dare not receive them. c.",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line005.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 6,
      "text": "GWW",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line006.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 7,
      "text": "Alexandria: December",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line007.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 8,
      "text": "L-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line008.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 9,
      "text": "5th. To John Robinson Esquire, Speaker.",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line009.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 10,
      "text": "The Bearer, Caplain fohn Mercer,",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line010.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 11,
      "text": "having teave to go down and Settle his Ac-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line011.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 12,
      "text": "compts with the Committee; is ordered to",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line012.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 13,
      "text": "call upon you for the balance of the ten",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line013.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 14,
      "text": "thousand founds, which I believe we shall",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line014.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 15,
      "text": "want before another opportunity may offer;",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line015.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 16,
      "text": "this being the time when our Demands for",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line016.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 17,
      "text": "money are greatest. I When Pleft Willi-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line017.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 18,
      "text": "amsburgh, I intended to proceed to Winches-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line018.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 19,
      "text": "ter; but meeting with Letters at Fredericks-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line019.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 20,
      "text": "burgh, informing me that peace prevailed",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line020.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 21,
      "text": "above, and that nothing was immediate-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line021.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 22,
      "text": "ly wanted but Salt; I came up here to en-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line022.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 23,
      "text": "gage what I could, und to wait the arrival",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line023.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 24,
      "text": "of some Recruits at this place; and a Vessel",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line024.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 25,
      "text": "with sundry trms, c. for the Troops. Shis Vef-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line025.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 26,
      "text": "sel left Williamsburgh two days after Idid,",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line026.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 27,
      "text": "and is not yet arrived: neither isthe Ex.-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line027.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 28,
      "text": "press returned, which the Governor sent to",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line028.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 29,
      "text": "Geneial Shirley for Commissions for the",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line029.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 30,
      "text": "Field officers of our Regiment: which gives,",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line030.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 31,
      "text": "me much concern; fearing that this de-",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line031.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 32,
      "text": "lay is ominous. In that case, I shall no",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line032.png"
    },
    {
      "page_index": 0,
      "line_index": 33,
      "text": "know how to act,- it will be useless for me",
      "crop_path": "line_images/304/304_line033.png"
    }
  ]
